# Cursor Rules for Transport Stack Hackathon 2026

Please read and strictly follow AGENTS.md at the root of this repository.

Key directives:
1. Environment & Tests:
   - Always verify changes with: PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/pytest tests/test_engine.py -v
   - Never commit .env or expose DELHI_GTFS_RT_API_KEY.
2. Design & Taste Standards (Anti-Slop Protocol):
   - Review .agents/skills/frontend-design, .agents/skills/emil-design-eng, .agents/skills/apple-design, .agents/skills/web-design-guidelines, and .agents/skills/review-animations before modifying UI code.
   - Avoid generic AI slop: no purple-on-white gradients, no default rounded card kits, no generic Inter/Roboto typefaces.
   - Tactile feedback: zero tap latency, scale down (scale: 0.97) on pointerdown/:active.
   - Motion budget: strictly < 300ms, GPU-only transforms (transform, opacity), transform-origin at click point.
3. Transit Engineering:
   - Preserve Delhi-specific transit factors (1.35x pink pass multiplier, Hensher-Wardman VOT, diurnal speed models).
